atus\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"An ed25519 CA keypair was generated at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca(.pub) on node1 via ssh-keygen, confirmed present with correct permissions.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-6d6d89961cd04004\"]},{\"id\":\"host-cert-signed\",\"requirement\":\"Host key signed by the CA to produce a host certificate\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1's ed25519 host public key was signed by the CA with principals node1 and its IP and a 10-year validity, producing /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub; ssh-keygen -L confirms the cert's signing CA fingerprint matches the generated CA.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-dce7b55fc1b2443d\"]},{\"id\":\"sshd-presents-cert\",\"requirement\":\"sshd on node1 configured to present the signed certificate to clients\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A HostCertificate directive was added via sshd_config.d drop-in, validated with sshd -t/-T (hostcertificate resolved to the correct path), and sshd was restarted; the certificate was subsequently observed to be presented in live handshakes.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-6257e998e9ee476a\",\"cmd-ce10a98634d640ff\",\"cmd-67ba57109f164628\"]},{\"id\":\"client-trusts-ca-no-pinning\",\"requirement\":\"A client that trusts the CA (not the host key) connects without pinning the host key, under strict host-key checking\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"With StrictHostKeyChecking=yes and an empty known_hosts, the connection failed as expected ('Host key verification failed'), establishing the baseline. With only an '@cert-authority' line for the CA public key (no pinned host key) in known_hosts, the same strict connection succeeded (EXIT=0), and verbose debug output confirms the server presented the ED25519-CERT host certificate and the client matched it via the CA, directly demonstrating the required outcome.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e52e449602f14111\",\"cmd-94ac659f7735408f\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-persistence\",\"requirement\":\"(Independent restart-evidence protocol, not 